# Exits on a zone master room and global exits in the master room (src/game.c process_command remote_exit and
# global_exit; src/move.c move_wrapper). A typed exit name and `goto` try the room's own exits, then the zone master
# room's, then the master room's. Rooms are found by name with lsearch(), never by literal dbref. Each check prints
# the mover's location by name, which reads the same on both servers.
::case rx.setup  a zone master room, a room zoned to it, and rooms to reach
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
::as wiz
@power me=No_Pay
think set(me,RXHOME:[loc(me)])
@dig RXZone
@dig RXHere
@dig RXThere
@dig RXLocal
@dig RXElsewhere
@chzone [lsearch(all,name,RXHere)]=[lsearch(all,name,RXZone)]
@open RXGate=[lsearch(all,name,RXThere)],,[lsearch(all,name,RXZone)]
@open RXGoto=[lsearch(all,name,RXThere)],,[lsearch(all,name,RXZone)]
@open RXShadow=[lsearch(all,name,RXThere)],,[lsearch(all,name,RXZone)]
@open RXShadow=[lsearch(all,name,RXLocal)],,[lsearch(all,name,RXHere)]
@open RXGlobal=[lsearch(all,name,RXElsewhere)],,[config(master_room)]

::case rx.zone-exit  typing a zone master room's exit takes it
@tel me=[lsearch(all,name,RXHere)]
RXGate
think [name(loc(me))]

::case rx.zone-goto  goto takes a zone master room's exit
@tel me=[lsearch(all,name,RXHere)]
goto RXGoto
think [name(loc(me))]

::case rx.zone-shadow  the room's own exit wins over the zone's exit of the same name
@tel me=[lsearch(all,name,RXHere)]
RXShadow
think [name(loc(me))]

::case rx.global-exit  typing a global exit takes it
@tel me=[lsearch(all,name,RXHere)]
RXGlobal
think [name(loc(me))]
@tel me=[v(RXHOME)]
